  "english": "8. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK / Tone 2 Plagal]. Ninth. Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 4 [BK]:\n\"Christ arose\" (Zkristos yareav), and the Morning [hymn].\n15. Sunday, Tone 3 [BDZ / Tone 2]. Tenth. Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 3 [B3]:\n\"The tidings of the messenger\" (Zayn avetavor), to the end.\nEve of the Fast of the Fifty [Yisnakats].\n16. Monday, Tone 4 [BK / Tone 2 Plagal]. Fast of the Fifty. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 3 [B1]:\n\"God most high\" (Astvats bardzryal).\n21. Saturday, Tone 1 [ADZ / Tone 1]. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n22. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK / Tone 1 Plagal]. First [Sunday of the Fifty]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 1 [ADZ]:\n\"Blessed art thou, Lord God\" (Orhnyal es ter astvats). Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 2 [AK]:\n\"Resurrected\" (Yarutsyal), and \"The wondrous angel\" (Sqancheli hreshtakn).\n23. Monday, Tone 3 [BDZ / Tone 2]. [Feast of Saints] Juliana and Vasilis. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]:\n\"Holy God, Creator\" (Surb astvats ararich).\n25. Wednesday, Tone 5 [GDZ / Tone 3]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 7 [D3]:\n\"Thou who in all...\"\n29. Sunday, Tone 1 [ADZ / Tone 1]. Second. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]:\n\"Who for our salvation\" (Vor vasn meroy prkutyan). Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn:\n\"Ineffable\" (Vor anchar). And the rest see according to the order.\n\nDecember.\n\n5. Saturday, Tone 7 [DDZ / Tone 4]. [Feast of Saints] Gregory and Nicholas the wonderworking bishops,\nand the other Nicholas the bishop,\nand Myron the bishop. Canticle of the Ascension [Mankunk]:\n\"They amazed\" (Hiatsan). Midday [Liturgy] Patristic Hymn Tone 5 [G3]:\n\"Who with light\" (Vor lusov).\n6. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK / Tone 4 Plagal]. Third. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [B3]:\n\"Incorruptible\" (Anapakan). Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 8 [DK]:\n\"Thy angel, Lord\" (Hreshtak qo ter). Eve of the Fast of Saint James [Hakob].\n9. Wednesday, Tone 3 [BDZ / Tone 2]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n13. Sunday, Tone 7 [DDZ / Tone 4]. Fourth. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]:\n\"Without beginning, God\" (Anskizbn astvats). Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 5 [GDZ]:\n\"Who art above\" (Vor i verd es).\n20. Sunday, Tone 6 [GK / Tone 3 Plagal]. Fifth. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [B3]:\n\"Glorified Son\" (Paravoryal vordi). Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 6 [GK]:\n\"With the divine tomb\" (Zastvatsayin zgerezmanavn), to the end.\n21. Monday, Tone 7 [DDZ / Tone 4]. [Feast of Saints] Abraham and Khoren, etc. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [G3]:\n\"Who the torments\" (Orq ztanjanšn).\n22. Tuesday, Tone 8 [DK / Tone 4 Plagal]. [Feast of Saint] Adeodatus [Astvatsatur] the martyr.\nCanticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [G3]:\n\"Those who hoped\" (Yusatsyalqn).\n24. Thursday, Tone 2 [AK / Tone 1 Plagal]. [Feast of] David the prophet, and James the Apostle.\n27. Sunday, Tone 5 [GDZ / Tone 3]. Sixth. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 6 [GK]:\n\"Pre-eternal\" (Naxahavitean). Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 5 [G3]:\n\"Glorified is thy...\" (Paravoryal e qo), to the end.\n29. Tuesday, Tone 7 [DDZ / Tone 4]. [Feast of the] Sons of Thunder, James and John. Eve of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Wednesday, Tone 8 [DK / Tone 4 Plagal]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ.\nCanticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 8 [DK]:\n\"God of our fathers, have mercy\" (Astvats hartsn merots oghormya). And the rest according to the order.\n\nJanuary.\n\n3. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK / Tone 2 Plagal]. Seventh, Fast. Resurrection [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 4 [BK]:\n\"They anticipated\" (Kanxetsin), to the end.\n5. Tuesday, Tone 6 [GK / Tone 3 Plagal]. Eve [Jragaluyts] of the Nativity of Christ.",
